# p4wn core

p4wn converts PDFs into PNG/HTML so specs and source material are easier to
understand. Readable conversion is the north star—not a full PDF product.

## Names

- Module: `p4wn` (code under `go-app-api/`)
- Binaries: `p4wn`, `p4wn-server`
- Run commands from the **repo root** (`go.work`)

## Stance

- `api/`, `cmd/`, docs, `testtools/`: change when the task asks
- `internal/*`: small, test-backed fixes only unless the user asks for fidelity
  or architecture work
- Known degradations in `go-app-api/README.md` stay known unless asked to fix
- Prefer fixtures under `testdata/` over ad-hoc scripts
- Keep diffs scoped to the request

## Hard rules

- Do not commit `data/` job artifacts
- Do not introduce Node/npm
- After Go changes: run relevant `go test p4wn/...`
- Visual changes: regenerate goldens only with `-update` and only intentionally
- Point to `AGENTS.md` and `go-app-api/README.md` for architecture depth—do not
  invent parallel design docs in chat
